abstract: >-
  causalbase learns the structure of Bayesian networks from data. Every search
  takes every score: BDeu or BIC on categorical data, the Gaussian BIC or BGe
  on continuous data. The searches are greedy equivalence search (GES) and
  XGES, iterated local search over variable orders, FLOP, hill climbing and
  tabu search over DAGs, and exact search by dynamic programming or integer
  programming; RCD, HC-LiNGAM and HC learn linear non-Gaussian models from
  higher-order cumulants. Scores and graph routines are compiled with Numba.
  Structural metrics, BIF and XMLBIF input, forward sampling, five bundled
  benchmark networks and the download of 226 more from Zenodo are included.
  fedcausal, which learns from data split across sites, is built on it.
keywords:
  - causal discovery
  - structure learning
  - Bayesian networks
  - greedy equivalence search
  - BDeu
  - order search
